{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdVaxPRPFsxYen4V4bkN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DHnZa1xCAHU594rMDPL1NS","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"Both problems are fixed. Global categories (project id 0, ALL_PROJECTS) can now be added, updated and deleted through the category commands, and the REST API ignores the old `status` field. A new helper, `category_parse_project_id()` in core/category_api.php, accepts project id 0 and keeps the old checks for other values (not numeric, below 1, unknown project). The add, update and delete commands use it. The delete rules did not change. The default category still cannot be deleted, and a category used by issues still cannot be deleted without reassignment. Both rules are now also tested for global categories. A global category cannot be reached through a normal project id, and a project category cannot be reached through project id 0. The add and update commands no longer read a `status` payload. Only `enabled` controls the state, so a REST `status` is ignored: a new category stays enabled, and an update with only `status` changes nothing. Responses never had `status` and still do not. I removed `status` from the ProjectCategoriesAdd and ProjectCategoriesUpdate schemas in the OpenAPI file. SOAP does not change: it never sent `status` to these commands, and the SOAP tests pass. To run the suite I started a temporary MySQL 8.0 container and a PHP server on 127.0.0.1:8989, installed MantisBT with the steps from the CI workflow, and created a new API token in tests/bootstrap.php. Afterwards I removed the container, stopped the server and restored tests/bootstrap.php. Nothing was committed.","changes":[{"path":"core/category_api.php","summary":"Added category_parse_project_id(): accepts ALL_PROJECTS (0), otherwise uses helper_parse_id() and checks that the project exists."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryAddCommand.php","summary":"Uses category_parse_project_id() so global categories can be added; removed the `status` payload override, only `enabled` (default true) is used."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryUpdateCommand.php","summary":"Uses category_parse_project_id(); removed the `status` payload override, only `enabled` is used (unchanged if missing)."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryDeleteCommand.php","summary":"Uses category_parse_project_id() so global categories can be deleted (by id or name); delete rules unchanged."},{"path":"api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml","summary":"Removed `status` from the ProjectCategoriesAdd and ProjectCategoriesUpdate request schemas."},{"path":"tests/Mantis/CategoryCommandTest.php","summary":"New tests: global add/update/delete, global delete by name, project/global boundary, invalid project ids still rejected, `status` payload ignored."},{"path":"tests/Mantis/CategoryDeleteCommandTest.php","summary":"New tests: default global category cannot be deleted; global category with issues cannot be deleted without reassignment."},{"path":"tests/rest/RestProjectCategoryTest.php","summary":"New tests: REST ignores `status` on add/update and never returns it; global category CRUD via /projects/0/categories."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"A global category can be added, updated and deleted through the commands, and REST ignores `status`","met":true,"evidence":"CategoryCommandTest::testGlobalCategoryAddUpdateDelete, testGlobalCategoryDeleteByName and RestProjectCategoryTest::testGlobalCategoryCrud pass. CategoryCommandTest::testStatusFieldIsIgnored and RestProjectCategoryTest::testProjectCategoryStatusFieldIsIgnored pass: a new category stays enabled, an update with only `status` leaves it enabled, and no response contains `status`. The default-category rule still applies to global categories (testCannotDeleteDefaultGlobalCategory)."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"Added 7 command tests and 2 REST tests. With the origin